# Monorepo Agent Rules — CubeCom

Canonical source: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Keep this file aligned with it.

You are in a production monorepo. Do not treat each app as an isolated project.

Default behavior:

1. Understand package boundaries
2. Reuse shared packages first
3. Preserve visual and architectural consistency
4. Avoid app-local duplication
5. Make the smallest coherent change

## Before implementing

Inspect `packages/*` and sibling apps first. Prefer existing:

- `@repo/ui` primitives (`Button`, `Section`, `Heading`, `Typography`, `Stack`, `Grid`, `List`, `Card`, …)
- `@repo/tailwind-config` tokens
- `@repo/fonts`
- `@repo/graphql` / `@repo/product-graph` / related contracts

Do not create `LandingButton`, app-local color/type scales, or duplicated Tailwind recipes when a shared primitive exists.

## Ownership

```text
apps → shared feature packages → ui / contracts / config
```

- Apps compose packages; packages never import apps
- Prefer `import { … } from '@repo/ui'` over deep `packages/.../src` paths
- Domain business logic stays out of `packages/ui`
- Promote to shared only when generic, reusable, and domain-neutral
- Keep page-specific compositions (proof demos, diagrams, 3D scenes) app-local

## Design system

- Tokens: `packages/tailwind-config`
- Fonts: `packages/fonts`
- Primitives: `packages/ui`
- Surfaces: `canvas` | `surface` | `soft` | `ink` — use inheritance, not hardcoded `#0c0c0f`
- Typography: `Heading` / `Typography` / shared variants — no parallel type stacks
- Actions: shared `Button` (polymorphic link when needed)
- Layout: `Container` / `Section` / `Stack` / `Grid` / `List` — do not recreate `max-w-[90rem] px-5 md:px-8`

## Change discipline

- Tailwind is for unique composition, not recreating primitives
- Preserve section rhythm, container width, radius, Button language, violet accent behavior
- Bad/off-brand visuals: remove + keep media slot / blank placeholder — no fake HTML artwork
- Responsive: 390 / tablet / laptop / desktop; `min-w-0` on grid children when needed
- After shared package edits: rebuild (`yarn workspace @repo/ui build`) and typecheck
- Do not hide errors (`ignoreBuildErrors`, blanket `any`, silenced lint)
- Migrate: preserve behavior → reuse/extend primitive → migrate call sites → remove local dup → verify

## After editing

Report files changed, shared packages reused, new shared APIs, validation run, and known/pre-existing failures.

**Golden rule:** reuse shared packages by default. Apps compose the platform; they do not recreate it.
